  <title>workspace-hub Gmail Filters — 2026-04-27</title>
  <!--
    Source runbook: docs/email/2026-04-27-filter-installation-runbook.md
    Derivation: 50-thread sample of owner@example.com inbox, 2026-04-27
    Companion issue: https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2529 (daily tracker)

    PREFLIGHT (do this before importing, in this order):
      1. Settings → Inbox → uncheck "Override filters for important"
         (without this, Skip-Inbox silently no-ops on important-classified mail —
         see feedback memory `feedback_gmail_override_filters_silent_defeat.md`)
      2. Create a new label called `gh-dependabot` in the Gmail UI
         (Gmail's filter import does NOT auto-create labels — Group 6 will fail
         to apply if this label doesn't exist yet)
      3. Settings → Filters and Blocked Addresses → "Import filters"
         → upload this file → review each entry → check "Apply filter to existing
         conversations" if you want immediate cleanup → Create filters

    Behavior notes:
      - Group 5 (Trello deleted-account bot) uses shouldTrash because the
        runbook flags this as immediate-delete (account is gone, no recovery
        path). All other groups use shouldArchive (safer; reversible).
      - Group 3 (industry feeds) intentionally omits shouldMarkAsRead so
        weekly skim of O&G Industry label stays easy.
      - Existing user labels assumed to exist: AutoNoise, CRE, O&G Industry.
        These were verified present via Gmail MCP list_labels on 2026-04-27.
  -->

